From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:41:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] media: mediatek: camraw: Frame done after the next
 start of frame

The one error of the first V4L2 run with the hard-IRQ timing was a CQ
trigger delay (INT b18) 0.13 ms after the second start of frame, right
after the per-frame lists were started for frame 3; there were 13 starts
of frame and 12 frame dones, and the first frames of a stream are long.
The frame done of frame 1 most likely came after the start of frame 2,
so the lists were started while the engine was still finishing a frame.
The same case also completed the wrong buffer: a late done was taken for
the frame that had just started.

- A frame done that comes after the next start of frame now ends the
  frame before (its own buffer, sequence and time stamp).
- While that done is outstanding, the per-frame application of the new
  start of frame is held back until it arrives (apply_wait, default on),
  at most until the next start of frame; a frame whose done never comes
  returns its buffer with an error.
- The start-of-frame log records each frame's done time; the counters
  show late dones and held-back applications, so the next run shows
  whether this was the cause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
